1.3 
policy
  mapping from percieved states of env -> actions to be taken
reward signal
  the only goal. the primary basis for altering the policy
value function
  reward signal: immdeiate. value function: long run
  value of a state: the total reward an agent can expect to accumulate over the future from that stateo
  
  reward: plaesure/pain. value function: farsighted prediction of reward
  values drive decisions, because thats how we get most reward.
  value estimation is core and difficult

  reminds me of working out: low reward (hurts), high value (will eventually lead to pussy)


model
  mimics behavior of environment. 
  given state/action, produce next state/next reward
  
model (optional)
